---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { products, productLink } from '../lib/gear';
import { absoluteUrl, formatTitle } from '../lib/utils';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/seo';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
const description = 'Build a sensory outing kit from familiar items. Compare fit, sound, portability and no-purchase alternatives before choosing equipment.';
const jsonLd = [breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', url: absoluteUrl('/', Astro.site) },
  { name: 'Sensory kit guide', url: absoluteUrl('/sensory-gear/', Astro.site) },
])];
---
<BaseLayout title={formatTitle('Sensory Outing Kit: What to Check Before Buying')} description={description} canonicalPath="/sensory-gear/" jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Sensory kit guide' }]} />
    <h1 class="mt-6 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">Build a sensory outing kit that fits your child</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">Start with one situation you want to plan for: a wait, unfamiliar lighting, noise, or asking for a break. Choose familiar items your child already uses and keep the bag small enough to carry when you need to leave.</p>
    <p class="mt-5 rounded-card border border-line bg-surface-soft p-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">This is a comparison of product types and practical packing choices. We have not personally tested or independently verified the products in retailer search results. General NIDCD and CPSC guidance linked below was checked September 7, 2026; that check does not certify an individual product.</p>

    <section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">Before adding anything to the bag</h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5">
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Ask about the venue.</strong> Check bag restrictions, available loans, a place for breaks, and whether you can return after stepping outside.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Offer a choice at home.</strong> Let your child decide whether an item's feel, sound, weight, or appearance is acceptable before relying on it during a trip.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Check the actual product.</strong> Read age limits, fit instructions, care requirements, and current recall information. A category name such as “sensory” does not establish suitability.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-ink">Keep an alternative.</strong> Decide how you will take a break or finish if the item does not help. Equipment is only one part of the outing.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">Hearing protection and toy selection</h2>
      <p><a class="link-underline text-brand-strong" href="https://www.nidcd.nih.gov/health/protect-your-childs-hearing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NIDCD's hearing guide</a> explains that protection depends on proper fit and use; no protector blocks all sound. Music headphones and protective earmuffs serve different purposes, so check the manufacturer's stated use instead of relying on an appearance or marketing label.</p>
      <p><a class="link-underline text-brand-strong" href="https://www.cpsc.gov/Safety-Education/Safety-Education-Centers/Toys" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CPSC's toy guidance</a> covers age suitability and small parts. We do not include water beads in this kit: <a class="link-underline text-brand-strong" href="https://www.cpsc.gov/Safety-Education/Safety-Education-Centers/Water-Beads-Information-Center" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CPSC warns about serious ingestion hazards</a>. This guide also does not prescribe weighted, compression, oral-motor, or sleep equipment; suitability needs an individual assessment beyond a shopping list.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">Compare seven simple options</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted"><strong class="text-ink">Affiliate disclosure:</strong> As an Amazon Associate, {SITE.name} earns from qualifying purchases. The optional links below open retailer searches, which may include ads and unsuitable results. Compare the seller's full details yourself; you can use this guide without buying anything.</p>
      <div class="mt-6 space-y-5">
        {products.map((product) => (
          <section id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 rounded-card border border-line bg-surface p-5 sm:p-6">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-brand-strong">{product.category}</p>
            <h3 class="mt-1 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">{product.name}</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted">{product.useCase}.</p>
            <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
              <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">What to check</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{product.blurb}</dd></div>
              <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Before buying</dt><dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{product.alternative}</dd></div>
            </dl>
            <a href={productLink(product)} target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer" class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm font-medium text-brand-strong link-underline">Optional: compare retailer search results →</a>
          </section>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 max-w-3xl space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-muted">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">Review the kit after a visit</h2>
      <p>Record what your child chose to use, what stayed in the bag, and what was difficult to reach. Remove unnecessary items before the next outing. Check anything worn or damaged against its instructions and keep communication tools available even if the rest of the kit changes.</p>
      <p>For a correction to this guide, <a href="/contact/" class="link-underline text-brand-strong">send us the detail and its official source</a>. Our <a href="/how-we-verify/" class="link-underline text-brand-strong">research process</a> explains what a source check means. Then <a href="/cities/" class="link-underline text-brand-strong">find an outing near you</a> and check the venue's specific accommodations.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
